RD05 native DSA v37 hardware-feedback notes

Topology
--------
RTL8197F physical P0/RGMII <-> RTL8367D CPU7/EXT1.
Linux DSA owns the 8-byte rtl8_4 tag, bridge, VLAN, FDB and STP state.
RTL8197F hardware tag insertion/removal stays disabled; both CPU-tag gates are
enabled so the complete tag reaches the Linux DSA tagger.

V37 evidence-based corrections
------------------------------
1. RTL8367D family-D register 0x13f9[5:3] is the EXT1 fine RGMII TX-clock tap.
   It is now independently configurable as rd05_ext1_txc_tap=0..7.
2. Register 0x13f7 synchronizer TX/RX error state and CPU7 CRC_SKIP are logged.
   CRC_SKIP remains clear; physical errors are not hidden.
3. RTL8197F irqchip parent numbering is offset for actual MIPS IRQ values.
4. rtl865x table seeding waits for SWCORE reset defaults.
5. SPI-NOR WEL calibration runs before rootfs_data partition registration.

Calibration
-----------
Router -> switch:
  rd05-rgmii-calibrate tx-auto save

Switch -> router, with continuous PC traffic for at least 240 seconds:
  PC:     sudo ./rd05-pc-netdiag.py --interface IFACE --configure-ip \
            --calibration --duration 240
  Router: rd05-rgmii-calibrate rx-auto save

The RX sweep covers 2 coarse switch TX settings x 8 fine 0x13f9 taps x
8 RTL8197F RX taps = 128 candidates. Failure restores the previous profile.

Final test
----------
  rd05-v37-check
  rd05-netdiag full

Expected:
- no new CPU7 FCS/drop errors;
- eth0 interrupt count rises under traffic;
- rx_cdp_advanced or eth0 RX rises;
- rd05_rx_external or rd05_rx_arp rises;
- ping 192.168.1.1 succeeds;
- /overlay is JFFS2 from rootfs_data immediately after boot.
